{#- How each present character sounds: one block per NAMED entry that has an
    anchor. A nameless entry contributes nothing -- an unattributed anchor is
    the very defect this section exists to fix.

    Carries its OWN heading rather than sharing one with voice_examples.j2 via
    a macro. The off-scene cast directory shares one that way and it is broken:
    it decides ownership from DATA (`if not offscene_active`) while layout.py
    lets a reader disable and reorder any section, so disabling one half loses
    the heading entirely (#423). Any data-derived "am I first?" test has that
    defect, because the question is about the merged, enabled layout.

    Vars: cast_blocks. -#}
{%- set blocks = [] -%}
{%- for b in cast_blocks -%}
{%- if b.name and b.anchor -%}
{%- set _ = blocks.append("## " ~ b.name ~ "
" ~ b.anchor) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if blocks %}# Voice — how they sound

{{ blocks | join("

") }}
{%- endif -%}
